  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Thursday)\nIssued at 1214 AM CDT Fri Aug 28 2026\n\nUpper level ridge that has been centered across the Southwest US\nwill transition east and become centered over the Southeast for\nnext week. This has little effect for actual weather across West\nCentral Texas, with generally hot and dry conditions prevailing.\nHottest conditions will continue across the area north of I-20,\nwhich largely missed out on the rainfall yesterday (Thursday)\nevening. For areas north of I-20, afternoon highs climbing up\nabove the 100 degree mark look likely (which means that Abilene\nwill make a serious run at breaking their consecutive 100+ degree\nstreak by Monday). Farther south, higher dewpoints and moist soils\nwill make hitting 100 a little more difficult. Highs in the mid\nand upper 90s looks more likely for the Edwards Plateau and Hill\nCountry.",
